# {{name}}

A hanafubuki-agent plugin written in Rust and compiled to WebAssembly, with
the guest SDK [kardia-guest](https://crates.io/crates/kardia-guest) (MIT OR
Apache-2.0). It contributes a tool (`greet`), a context section
(`{{kind}}_status`) and an observer (`turn_finished`). `package/` is the
plugin the Agent installs; the Cargo project around it builds its module,
one file for every platform.

Build the module into the package:

```sh
rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown
cargo build --release --target wasm32-unknown-unknown
cp target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/{{kind}}.wasm package/{{name}}.wasm
```

Check it, start it once, then run it in the Agent and reload it at each new
build until Ctrl+C:

```sh
hanafubuki-agent plugins validate package --run
hanafubuki-agent plugins dev package
```

The module reaches nothing outside itself: no files, network or
environment, so it asks for no permissions. `runtime.limits` bounds what
each call may use (fuel, `timeoutMs`, `memoryBytes`).

See [Writing plugins](https://licyk.github.io/hanafubuki-agent/docs/writing-plugins/).
